==Dragon Token==
{{Main|Dragon Token}}
Upon the release of [[Updates/24|Update 24]], the [[Dragon (Classic)|old Dragon fruits]] (physical and equipped) were converted into [[Dragon Token]]s, which could be exchanged for a random {{Mythical}} fruit, (including Dragon East and West) when used. Players who got it could also use the [[Dragon (Classic)]] if they had a [[Dragon Token|Permanent Dragon Token]]. Permanent Dragon fruits were instead converted into [[Dragon Token|Permanent Dragon Tokens]], which could be exchanged for one of these four sets of items:
* '''Upgrade:''' A discount on purchasing the new permanent Dragon (making it {{Robux|2,400}} instead of {{Robux|5,000}}).
* '''Fruits:''' A [[Dough|Permanent Dough]] alongside a [[Flame|Permanent Flame]].
* '''Game Passes:''' Some [[Shop#Game_Passes|Game Passes]], such as x2 [[Money]], x2 boss Drops, x2 [[Mastery]], Fast [[Boats]], [[+1 Fruit Storage]] (3x), and [[Fragments]].
* '''Swordsman:''' A [[Dark Blade]], 2 [[Mythical Scroll|Mythical]] and 2 [[Legendary Scroll]]s, and some [[Fragments]].
After heavy backlash from the community, the [[Dragon Token|Dragon Tokens]] were changed three days after the update (December 17, 2024).
* After the change, everyone who had a physical Dragon were given one of either an Eastern or Western Dragon in physical form, with the rest of the regular Dragon Tokens being changed to randomly exchange to any of these {{Mythical}} fruits (with an equal chance): [[Shadow]], [[Dough]], [[Venom]], [[Gas]], [[Tiger]], [[Kitsune]] and Dragon.
* Permanent Dragon Tokens were instead removed, and everyone who had a permanent Dragon were instead able to choose to get either the Eastern or Western version permanently.
* Those who bought Permanent Dragon with the [[Dragon Token|Permanent Dragon Token's]] discount would have their Token returned in tradeable form.
* The [[Dragon (Classic)|old version of Dragon]] was made unobtainable.

